},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":410064485,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0MTAwNjQ0ODU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/needs%20testing","name":"needs testing","color":"ffcc44","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-08-24T01:44:12Z","updated_at":"2025-08-25T10:48:03Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7640) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-4790 CPU @ 3.60GHz (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen adding Sprite2Ds to a Skeleton2D using RemoteTransform2Ds that are placed after the Bone2D child of the respective Bone2D, it results in the offsets lagging behind and the sprites ending up all over the place.\nIt's especially noticeable after moving (or halting) fast.\n\nE.g.:\nThis works as expected:\n\n```\nSkeleton2D\n>UpperArmBone2D\n>>RemoteTransform2D\n>>LowerArmBone2D\n...\n```\n\nThis leads to the Sprite2D lagging behind, overextending, and not halting in the correct location/rotation:\n\n```\nSkeleton2D\n>UpperArmBone2D\n>>LowerArmBone2D\n>>RemoteTransform2D\n...\n```\n\nI wouldn't expect the order among siblings to affect the RemoteTransform2D's transform, nor the transform it passes on, in any way.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a Skeleton2D using RemoteTransform2D to control render order of the Sprite2Ds and change the child index of the RemoteTransform2D. If it comes before the Bone2D, it bugs out. \n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[remotetransformweirdness.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21954707/remotetransformweirdness.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109924/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109924/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}